{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of the peptide shows 47.2% similarity to Distinctin. Activity: Active against bacteria mainly Gram- E. coli (MIC 32 ug/mL), P. aeruginosa (MIC 64 ug/mL) and fungi C. albicans (MIC 64 ug/mL). Also inhibits proliferation of cancer cell lines such as H157, and PC3, but with little toxicity against normal human cell, HMEC-1.Predicted to be helical. The active region is located at the N-terminus of the peptide. Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "29628917", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2018 Mar 23;9:541. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2018.00541. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02976", "source_id": "AP02976", "source_numeric_id": "02976", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02976", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Discovery of Distinctin-Like-Peptide-PH (DLP-PH) From the Skin Secretion of Phyllomedusa hypochondrialis, a Prototype of a Novel Family of Antimicrobial Peptide", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
